! DBG113S.DBG - the scope round (README.md): what Phase 89's probe left open.
! VMS's log leaves out a command that fails, so a comment names each case first.
!> TYPE with no line, before any source has been shown
TYPE
SET BREAK INLEAF
GO
SHOW CALLS
!> The PSL in each scope: LEAF's live N and DV, then what each outer scope shows
EXAMINE PSL
EXAMINE 1\%PSL
EXAMINE 2\%PSL
EXAMINE 4\%PSL
EXAMINE 5\%PSL
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
EXAMINE PSL
EXAMINE/PSL PSL
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 4
EXAMINE/PSL PSL
CANCEL SCOPE
!> %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY at the last levels
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 4
EVALUATE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 5
SHOW SCOPE
EVALUATE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 6
SHOW SCOPE
EVALUATE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 7
SHOW SCOPE
EVALUATE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
CANCEL SCOPE
!> EXAMINE with no location after the PC, the PSL, SP, and AP
EXAMINE PC
EXAMINE
EXAMINE
EXAMINE PSL
EXAMINE
EXAMINE SP
EXAMINE
EXAMINE R11
EXAMINE
!> DEPOSIT to scope 2's R2 (saved in REC(1)'s frame) and R5 (saved by no frame)
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 2
DEPOSIT R2 = %HEX 2222
DEPOSIT R5 = %HEX 5555
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
!> DEPOSIT to scope 1's R6 (saved in LEAF's frame), and R2 (live)
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
DEPOSIT R6 = %HEX 6666
DEPOSIT R2 = %HEX 1212
EXAMINE R6
EXAMINE R2
!> DEPOSIT to scope 1's R0
DEPOSIT R0 = %HEX 1010
!> DEPOSIT to scope 1's SP
DEPOSIT SP = SP
!> DEPOSIT to scope 1's PSL
DEPOSIT PSL = PSL
!> DEPOSIT to scope 1's PC, the same value
DEPOSIT PC = DEEP
EXAMINE PC
!> Each register in scope 0 after the deposits
CANCEL SCOPE
EXAMINE R0
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
EXAMINE R6
EXAMINE 1\%R2
EXAMINE 1\%R6
EXAMINE 2\%R2
EXAMINE 2\%R5
!> After LEAF returns to REC(1): R6 from LEAF's frame, R2 and R5
SET BREAK DEEP
GO
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
EXAMINE R6
EXAMINE PSL
!> After REC(1) returns to REC(2): R2 from REC(1)'s frame
SET BREAK BACK
GO
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
EXAMINE R6
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
